A||||30||Fierochic88||Just When You Think Things Couldn't Get Worse...sister's friend murdered....||||9||
Z||000000||Fierochic88||07-12-2001||12:44 PM||||Well the boyfriend crisis seems to be receding but things far worse have occurred.  I haven't said anything about this the past few days because I was too in shock but now I'm even more upset and need to get it off my chest because I'm worried about my little sister.  The poor kid is only 18 and in the past month she has already lost one friend.  On Saturday morning, at 3 AM, she lost another.<P>Jamie's very close friend, Shawn, was shot execution style in his living room while he fell asleep watching TV.  Someone merely walked in his front door, shot him and walked out, all the while his parents and little brother were asleep upstairs.  Shawn was 24 and worked with Jamie.  After several off years after high school he had been taking classes at the local community college and was set to go to a university to pursue a physical therapy degree in the fall.  He was promised a position at the place he and Jamie work as assistants upon graduation.<P>From the words of his parents the past few days, and the local newspaper (scarily enough they mentioned his date with my sis!) Jamie was quickly becoming a bright spot in his life.  Though she has a bf they were really close friends and Shawn really liked her a lot.  Saturday they were supposed to go horseback riding together and Friday night while at the bar with his friends, that was all he talked about.  His phone call never came Saturday and Jamie was crushed, she was so looking forward to that as well as the DMB concert we were all going to in 3 weeks.  Monday morning, upon arrival at work, she heard the news.<P>Since then she hasn't eaten or slept too much.  She won't talk about it with anyone and is convinced that all her friends are gonna die (this was #5 in the last year).  Today, to make matters even worse, she is being questioned by the police.  She knows it is necessary to help them find Shawn's killer but she is still very scared and upset by it.  <P>Supposedly they have a strong lead but are lacking in evidence and the suspect has disappeared.  <P>I'm really worried about my sister and don't know what to do.  Anyone have any advice in dealing with this?<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||skitime||07-12-2001||12:56 PM||||Hey Jennifer very sorry to hear the awful news.  I know your whole family must be terribly upset too.  If you and your sister want to just get away, we are going to the shore camping and you both would be welcome to join us. Maybe some beach time will help heal the soul or at least soften the pain. Our prayers are with your sister and family.<P>Dave<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierobaby||07-12-2001||12:58 PM||||go give your sister a big hug from me. I have been in that boat loosing friends left and right. its a hard time. especially having to be questioned. I will pray for her and her friends family. its sad that someone can just go kill another human like that. do they have any idea for a reason he was killed? I hope they catch the killer and he is locked up for a very long time! life would be good!<P>I'll be praying for all of you!<BR>*big hug to all*<P>Corinne||||reg||9
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||07-12-2001||01:41 PM||||It's things like this that makes you wonder what the world is coming to.<P>I hope they will find the killer and that they will lock him away for the rest of his pathetic life.||||reg||8
Z||000004||fierohoho||07-12-2001||01:54 PM||||Fierochic88, you need to get your sister help in dealing with this loss. <P>Look in your phone book for a Crisis line and call them. <P>Ask their advise on how to talk to her about this loss, this is not something she should be bottling up. <P>If they have a support group, see if you can get her to go, and go with her. <P>Best of luck.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mach10||07-12-2001||02:13 PM||||I'm at loss for what to say. Normally, I can try to make light of any situation. So I thought. I can't express how horrible this must be. I'm sorry.<P>All I can really say is "be there." Sorry.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||KnightRyder31||07-12-2001||02:30 PM||||I hate to say it, but I do know how she feels.<BR>My cousin was murdered on Jan. 1st 2001 in Easton, PA.<BR>My cousin and I were like brothers...<BR>Its very hard to deal with.<BR>My cousin was only 22 years old, and some mother F***er shot my cousin Robert, after he pushed this kid out of the way of the bullet.<BR>There was only one bullet in the damn gun!<BR>I swear to God that if this piece of trash gets out of prison, and I hear about it, I'll kill him my self!<P><BR>All you can do is infact be there for your sister and the guys family.<BR>You can expect that his family will be messed up for a great deal of time.<BR>I am sorry.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fierochic88||07-12-2001||05:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>Hey Jennifer very sorry to hear the awful news.  I know your whole family must be terribly upset too.  If you and your sister want to just get away, we are going to the shore camping and you both would be welcome to join us. Maybe some beach time will help heal the soul or at least soften the pain. Our prayers are with your sister and family.<P>Dave</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Thanks for the offer.  What beach are you guys going too?  I may be going to Kick Hill but I think Jamie is going to the beach.  Maybe she can meet up with you guys.<P>Jen<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fierochic88||07-12-2001||05:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>My cousin was murdered on Jan. 1st 2001 in Easton, PA.<BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>That is near my house.  Bout 45 min away.  I'm sorry to hear about your cousin.  The world is a messed up place.<P>Jennifer<BR>||||reg||1
